A||||5||Leadfoot||Previous fiero owner and his comment||||8||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||09-07-2001||11:13 PM||||Back in around Feb. I bought my 85se (150,000 miles) from a friend.  The car was in bad shape...motor was weak, interior was torn up, supension bushings shot....yadda yadda yadda!  Well since then I have been spending most of my free time and money fixing her up.  Meanwhile I have been telling my friend about all that I have done to the car and I just found out from another friend that he thinks I am an idiot.  He said no way would he every be dumb enough to spend that kind of money on a car like that.  This kinda ticked me but I figured he is sort of right since I needed this car like a hole in the head.  Well today I found out that this same gut just spent $8k on an 82 944.  WTF!  Isn't he the one that is nuts?  I bought the fiero from him for about $900 and have yet to invest $4k into it.  I want so very badly to race him now.  I just want to know what are my chances of beating him considering I have a fresh 2.8?  Boy would I love to see his face in my rear view mirror as I am laughing my a$$ off.     ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Raydar||09-07-2001||11:26 PM||||He spent $8K on an 82 944 and he's calling *you* an idiot?!<BR>I think he's got rocks in his head.<P>Not sure if you'll take him in a race. You won't if it's been turbo'd.<P>Funny that you should mention this. My wife wants a 944. There's one on e-bay with a toasted motor. Only up to a grand. Would make a perfect home for a small block Chevy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Leadfoot||09-07-2001||11:32 PM||||I don't think it has a turbo.  I knew a guy at school that had one and after 2 months he got rid of it.  Darn thing wanted to be a bird since it was up on the jack so many times.  From what I understand the bolts holding the cv together kept breaking.  Man! for $8k I could have bought a body kit from Archie, installed a 3.4 and still have enough to buy a slurpy.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||09-07-2001||11:37 PM||||Just wait 'til he starts pricing Porshe parts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||TopFiero||09-07-2001||11:46 PM||||  A stock naturally aspirated Porsche 944 in good shape will hit 0-60 in about 8.3-8.5 seconds and the 1.4-mile in 16.4-16.7 seconds, so if you have a strong running motor and are a decent driver, you should be able to edge ahead.  ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||09-08-2001||12:07 AM||||944's with a N/A motor are dogs! Just remember they are also "interference" motors. A kid next door had one. He tried to race a Mustang, Blew a shift, toasted the timing belt, needed lots of head/engine work.<BR>I use to "toy" with him while I was driving a twin-cam Geo Storm.||||reg||1
